  "tagline": "Always-on Bots that share one cloud computer and work in your apps.",
  "description": "Grok Bot is SpaceXSI's always-on agent product, launched in beta on August 11, 2026 and run on Cursor: you sign in with a Cursor account, and access comes with The X Subscription, Cursor plans or a linked SuperGrok subscription. Each user gets one persistent cloud computer, a Linux Firecracker microVM hosted by Cursor in the United States, which all of that user's named Bots share, with its browser sessions, terminal and files; Bots keep working with the laptop closed, use connectors where they exist and computer use elsewhere, and hand passwords, two-factor codes and payment steps back to the user. You reach Bots in the desktop and mobile apps, by voice chat, by tagging @bot on X, in Slack for Team Bots, and at an optional address on mail.grokbot.com. Routines run on schedules or on events such as a Slack message or incoming email; Bots message each other, hand off work and launch subagents, and an independent review model (Auto Review) checks risky actions against the user's Ask first and Allow automatically rules. Cursor picks the model for each request from xAI's own models and third-party ones, with no model picker; its help page names Opus 5.5 as one of them. Recent additions include an iPhone Action Button shortcut for voice chat, Pages (reports, memos and dashboards the Bot builds, edits and shares) and a 1Password integration that fills approved logins without the Bot seeing them, the last two rolling out gradually. The agent harness, the other models, the routing, the voice stack and how memory is stored are not disclosed.",
